//
// A PARSE INTO A RECORD WITH A BARE ENUM FIELD NEEDS ITS DEFAULT (`@FR-D-NoEnumF` crossed with
// `@FR-N-Cast` and `@FR-N-Parse`).  N-Parse folds into N-Cast: "a parse is a cast", and a text
// parse into a struct leaves every misfit or missing field AT ITS DEFAULT (STDLIB.md
// `record#errors`, @C148).  D-NoEnumF: a bare enum field without `= expr` HAS no default, and
// "the partiality is a TYPE rule": where a cast would need the default of such a record —
// `s as Tinted` on a variant — the cast is refused at compile time.  A parse needs the same
// default for every field the text omits, so `t as NpPixel` must be refused the same way.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: has no default: field `tint: NpColour`
//
// @falsified-at: 18594597b (loft#2079) — it compiles and answers `{tint:null,x:4}` on both backends.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic (absent on 18594597b).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the record prints `{tint:null,x:4}`.
// HOLDS: `a-variant-cast-needing-a-default-of-a-bare-enum-field-is-refused` beside it.

enum NpColour { Red, Green }
struct NpPixel { tint: NpColour, x: integer }

fn main() {
  t = "{{\"x\":4}}";
  w = t as NpPixel;
  assert(w.tint != null && w.x == 4, "a non-null enum field read null: {w}");
}
